    "id": "rate_half_ca_hankel_a1_first_degree_core_one_quadratic_gap_four_paired_zero_excess_first_jet_transversality",
    "title": "A=1 quadratic paired zero-excess first-jet transversality",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "exact support-root first jet and paired curve coprimality",
    "statement": "At every actual-support root of every selected zero-excess fiber, the contracted full locator and paired split-biform curves are smooth and transverse. The exact first-jet mismatch is the nonzero actual error times the dual and locator weights; the nonincidence Forney constant controls only the minimum-word summand. Padding then makes the extremal curves coprime and reduces every strict common component to an X-linear parameter-high factor. A classified row/fiber incidence count excludes that final factor, so the full locator and split biform are coprime in both paired profiles.",
